Router module: proven root cause and workaround
================================================

Problem: dynamically swapping routers via KontrolRack_loadmodule() does
not produce audio. This affects ALL routers, not just hybrid-sndsel.

Root cause (proven):
- KontrolRack_loadmodule() (KontrolRack.cpp:460-475) clears the s1
  subpatch and rebuilds it with r~ inL-s1 / s~ outL-s1 wired to the
  module's inlet~/outlet~.
- The router's internal r~ oinL / throw~ ooutL still receive/send audio
  (global names), but fullmodule instances inside the new router have
  uninitialized delComp state: sig~ (bypass multiplier) defaults to 0
  (mute). It only gets set to 1 when delComp's bng fires, which happens
  on `r bar` (transport) or `r loadbang-$1` (slot loadbang).
- After a router swap, the loader sends loadbang-s1, but fullmodule's
  delComp listens to loadbang-$1 where $1 = slot name (a1, a2, etc.),
  NOT s1. So delComp never initializes -> audio stays muted.
- Starting transport sends `bar`, which triggers delComp -> audio works.
  This is why sound only appears after transport start.

Attempted fixes:
- Adding dummy inlet~/outlet~ to module.pd: caused interference with
  DSP graph, made swapping worse (failed both directions instead of
  one).
- Forwarding loadbang-s1 to loadbang-a1..d4: triggered synth module
  reinitialization, all synths reset to default params.
- Sending fake `bar` on loadbang: side effect of starting transport /
  sequencers, causing unwanted sound.
- Local fullmodule.pd with sig~ 1 default: PD didn't pick up the local
  copy when module loaded via dynamic loader's absolute path.

Workaround (proven, in use):
- main.pd references hybrid-sndsel via absolute path:
    /sdcard/media/orhack/user-modules/routers/hybrid-sndsel/module
  with KontrolModule type "routers/hybrid-sndsel".
- Preset moduleType must match ("routers/hybrid-sndsel") so no dynamic
  swap is triggered. Presets using other routers (e.g. stock Hybrid)
  will swap and work after transport start.

Location:
- hybrid-sndsel lives in user-modules
  (/sdcard/media/orhack/user-modules/routers/hybrid-sndsel/) so it can
  be part of the orhack-usermodules git repo.
- The absolute path in main.pd is the only modification to the orhack
  patch itself.
- All presets (Denkmal, HeartOfGlass, Init, jam, new-3) in
  /sdcard/data/orhack/presets/ were changed to moduleType
  "routers/hybrid-sndsel" so no router swap is triggered when switching
  between presets.

